WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.560
Ever wondered why some people
seem to have all the luck?

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.720
We've been trying to improve
our luck for centuries -

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.000
lucky charms, amulets and talismans

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.120
have figured in virtually
every recorded civilization.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.360
Early Europeans believed
iron had magical qualities

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.760
so hanging horseshoes in your house
was meant to ward off spirits.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.600
Touching or knocking on wood is
said to date back to Celtic rituals

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.040
that were designed to rouse the tree
gods and call on their protection.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.600
Throughout history, people have
recognised that good and bad luck

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.000
can transform lives.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.240
A few seconds of bad luck can
overturn years of hard work

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.480
and moments of good luck
can save years of striving.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.200
Superstition represents
people's attempts

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.560
to improve and control their luck.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.320
British psychologist
and author Richard Wiseman

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.120
undertook a ten year study
on the science of luck.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.440
In one experiment he asked people
to look through a newspaper

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.840
and count the number
of photographs inside.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.920
On average it took the people who
thought of themselves as unlucky

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.120
around two minutes.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.960
People who thought of themselves
as lucky on the other hand

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.200
took a few seconds.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:09.960
Why?

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.480
Because on the second page
there was a message that said,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:13.680
in a massive font,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.160
"Stop counting, there are 43
photographs in this newspaper."

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.680
The lucky people it seems
were more open to possibilities

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.760
other than the ones
they were searching for.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.200
There are four main
psychological principles

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.800
that separate lucky people
from unlucky ones.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.240
So first of all, lucky people
are more open to opportunities,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.240
spotting them and making
the most of them.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.440
Second, they tend to be optimists

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.360
and that becomes
a self-fulfilling prophecy -

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.760
they're pushing forward,
they're expecting the best.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.440
Also differences
in terms of intuition -

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.840
lucky people tend
to have lucky hunches

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.520
and trust their intuition.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.520
And finally, they're more resilient.
When bad things happen,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.440
they're good at turning that
bad luck into good fortune.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.720
So big differences in the way they
think and the way they behave.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.240
But whilst it's true that
if you train hard

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.480
you are more likely
to win a sporting event,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.840
or the harder you swot for an exam
the more you increase your chances

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.680
of the best grade
you're capable of.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.520
Here's the kicker.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.760
No amount of positivity,
work or preparation

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.640
will reduce the chance of say,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.560
being kept awake by noisy neighbours
the night before an exam

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.680
or slipping on a wet patch
as you run during a race.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.760
It would be wrong to think that all
of someone's good or bad luck

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.480
is entirely due to the way
they're thinking and behaving.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.760
When it comes to people who aren't
quite so successful or happy in life

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.880
we shouldn't think
it's all their fault.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.160
It could be down to where they're
born or the society they're born into

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.440
or chance accidents or illnesses,

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.120
and you need to take
all of those factors into account.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.040
In 2012 at a campaign rally,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.640
Barack Obama caused
controversy when he said,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.480
"If you're successful,
you didn't get that on your own.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.000
If you're successful, somebody along
the line gave you some help."

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.240
And he raises a key factor
by considering the role of luck.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.000
There's a whole bunch
of hard-working,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.920
positive-thinking people out there

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.120
who aren't successful
and certainly aren't lucky.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:08.040
Obama's statement sparked debate,
with several online publications

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.960
railing against him,
and public figures

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.520
like republican rival Mitt Romney
openly rebuffing him.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.360
For many, Obama's comments were seen

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.640
as an insult to the
American work ethic

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.600
and the idea that success
was achieved through merit.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.400
But as the economist
Robert H. Frank argues,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.800
talent and drive will get you so far

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.800
but luck and life chances
will also play a huge role.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.680
What if you asked the question,
"Where do your talents come from?"

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.640
"Where does your propensity
to work hard come from?"

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.240
If you're a hard working person
who has a lot of talent

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.040
you got those traits from the
environment you grew up in

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.520
and from the genes you inherited.
You're not in any strict sense

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.120
in a position to claim
moral credit for them.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.880
And so we're comfortable
enough saying that

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.760
you're lucky to have those traits.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.400
But what about the person
who works hard?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.880
Is that person not entitled
to congratulate herself

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.400
for the effort she put forward?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.920
What we know is that
putting forth effort

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.240
in trying circumstances is difficult.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.520
It requires often a Herculean will

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.320
to go forward in the face
of one setback after another.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.800
If you're the kind of person
who's been taught that

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.040
your temperament alone determines
whether you'll be persistent

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.560
and your temperament
is just a matter of luck,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.480
I think you're more likely to sit
back and wait and see what happens.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.600
If instead you view yourself
as the captain of your own fate

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.000
and think, "It's up to me
to make it happen"

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.760
you're much more likely to persist
against a series of setbacks.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.480
So it's like Richard
Wiseman said earlier,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.800
lucky and unlucky people are often
determined by the way they think,

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.680
which suggests that
there is hope for change.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.680
I think that anyone has the
capability and the potential

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.480
to make themselves luckier.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.760
It's realising that
lots of that good fortune

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.320
is due to the way you're thinking,
the way you're behaving.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.600
Understand the mindset
of the lucky person

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.960
and you can bring more
good fortune into your life.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.900
Thanks for watching. Don't forget to subscribe

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.440
